ernative Learning System (ALS) emphasizes that the absence of sufficient facilities impacts the development of 21st-century life skills (Title: Implementation of ALS and 21st Century Life Skills)', 'The difficulties faced by Grade 11 TVL students due to the lack of facilities and equipment are significant. The absence of proper resources, such as learning materials and a conducive environment, hinders skill acquisition, particularly in fields requiring hands-on training (Title: Motivations and Challenges in Specializing TLE). Additionally, financial constraints and limited access to supplementary resources exacerbate the challenges (Title: Motivations and Challenges in Specializing TLE). A study on the implementation of the Alternative Learning System (ALS) emphasizes that the absence of sufficient facilities impacts the development of 21st-century life skills (Title: Implementation of ALS and 21st Century Life Skills)']}
